## Problem

`mergeCcSource` at `src/adapters/claude-code/cc-note.ts:146` carries forward only string entries from an existing `sources` array:

```
const push = (s: unknown) => {
  if (typeof s === "string" && s.length > 0 && !seen.has(s)) {
    seen.add(s);
    out.push(s);
  }
};
if (Array.isArray(existing)) for (const s of existing) push(s);
```

Any non-string entry in `sources` is silently dropped.

## Found running flatten across the prismalens hub

`decisions/0028-correlation-semantics.md` had `- issue: "prismalens/prismalens#244"`, an object-form entry, and it was dropped by `mergeCcSource` during flatten. Nothing was lost in this specific case only because the same issue number happened to survive separately as `provenance.issue`.

## Ask

A repair tool that runs across a whole knowledge base has to round-trip every shape it meets, not just the string form. Either preserve non-string `sources` entries through `mergeCcSource`, or fail loudly when one is encountered instead of dropping it.

Gate addition, approved by the operator on 2026-11-17 (RECON1). A release workflow runs `scripts/check_reconcile.sh` unmasked. This closes the gap behind spec-sweep rule T-5 (#6615, LAB #6861).

Today `release.yml`, `binary-release.yml` and `release-gates-nightly.yml` run it 0 times. The spec-sweep T-5 rule scans only `binary-release.yml` and `release-gates-nightly.yml`.

