If the party holds the jump key and jumps into water, it keeps bouncing across the water and takes no water damage. With the key held, the party can cross any body of water. Jumping into water should play the splash once and then stop the jumping, leaving the party in the water.

Reproduced on master at 993a5ecaf66 with a throwaway game test on Emerald Island. It starts a new game, teleports to the shore at grid (88, 24), world `(12032, 20224)`, facing east, then holds Up and X for 150 frames:

```cpp
game.teleportTo(MAP_EMERALD_ISLAND, Vec3f(12032, 20224, 1), 0);
game.pressKey(PlatformKey::KEY_UP);
game.pressKey(PlatformKey::KEY_X);
game.tick(150);
game.releaseKey(PlatformKey::KEY_X);
game.releaseKey(PlatformKey::KEY_UP);
game.tick(20);
```

What happens:
- Water starts at x=12800. The party bounces across it and reaches x=22528, 19 water tiles out, by frame 136. Then it keeps bouncing in place.
- On every landing z drops to the water surface (1 to 10) and the party jumps straight back up. `PARTY_FLAG_WATER_DAMAGE` never gets set and HP doesn't change.
- Two frames after X is released, the water damage flag gets set and HP starts dropping.

Likely cause, from reading `ProcessPartyActions` in `Outdoor.cpp` and not verified with a fix: `PARTY_Jump` is only blocked by `PARTY_FLAG_WATER_DAMAGE`, and that flag is cleared every frame and set again only after the jump action is handled. The jump also lifts the party by 1, so the `pos.z <= terrainHeight + 1` drowning check never passes on a landing frame while the key is held.

## Problem
`aws_api_gateway_deployment.api_deployment` in `apps/server/terraform/api_gateway.tf` has no `triggers` and no `create_before_destroy`. Terraform creates the deployment once and never again. Any later change to methods, integrations or CORS responses is applied to the REST API but **is not deployed to the stage**, so production silently stays on the old config.

## Suggested fix
```hcl
resource "aws_api_gateway_deployment" "api_deployment" {
  rest_api_id = aws_api_gateway_rest_api.api.id

  triggers = {
    redeployment = sha1(jsonencode([
      aws_api_gateway_resource.api_contact_resource,
      aws_api_gateway_method.api_contact_method,
      aws_api_gateway_integration.api_lambda_integration,
      aws_api_gateway_method.options_method,
      aws_api_gateway_integration.options_api_integration,
      aws_api_gateway_integration_response.options_api_integration_response,
    ]))
  }

  lifecycle {
    create_before_destroy = true
  }
}
```

