## Summary

When a struct with an embedded (anonymous) field crosses an `interface{}` boundary — e.g. stored in a `map[string]any` and handed to `text/template` — minigo can resolve the struct's **declared** fields but not **promoted** members of the embedded field. `gc` resolves both.

## Repro

```go
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"os"
	"text/template"
)

type Moderation struct {
	Hidden       bool
	HiddenReason string
}

type Comment struct {
	ID   int64
	Body string
	Moderation
}

func dict(pairs ...any) map[string]any {
	m := make(map[string]any, len(pairs)/2)
	for i := 0; i+1 < len(pairs); i += 2 {
		m[pairs[i].(string)] = pairs[i+1]
	}
	return m
}

func main() {
	c := &Comment{ID: 1, Body: "hi", Moderation: Moderation{Hidden: true, HiddenReason: "spam"}}
	for _, src := range []string{
		"direct: {{.C.ID}} {{.C.Body}}",
		"promoted: {{.C.Hidden}} {{.C.HiddenReason}}",
		"explicit: {{.C.Moderation.Hidden}} {{.C.Moderation.HiddenReason}}",
	} {
		t := template.Must(template.New("t").Parse(src))
		if err := t.Execute(os.Stdout, dict("C", c)); err != nil {
			fmt.Printf("%s => ERROR: %v\n", src, err)
			continue
		}
		fmt.Println()
	}
}
```

## Results

`go run .` (gc):

```
direct: 1 hi
promoted: true spam
explicit: true spam
```

`minigo run .`:

```
direct: 1 hi
promoted: promoted: {{.C.Hidden}} {{.C.HiddenReason}} => ERROR: template: t:1:14: executing "t" at <.C.Hidden>: can't evaluate field Hidden in type interface {}
explicit: true spam
```

So the failure is specific to the **promoted-member lookup through an interface boundary**: `.C.ID`/`.C.Body` and the explicit `.C.Moderation.*` path work, `.C.Hidden` does not. (Promoted methods are presumably affected the same way, though I only verified fields.)

## Real-world impact

Found via the storybook in `podhmo/go-classic-mpa-sample`, which interprets `internal/web` with minigo: adding an embedded `Moderation` struct to the comment types and referencing `.C.Hidden` in `html/template` made every commen

